        <h2 class="section-title">Composability vs. Reversibility</h2>
        <p class="section-subtitle">
          Why these two execution modes are mutually exclusive &mdash; and why that is exactly the point.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 max-w-4xl mx-auto mb-10" data-reveal-stagger>
        <!-- Composability -->
        <div class="accent-card">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-primary/10 flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-primary" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M4 6h16M4 10h16M4 14h16M4 18h16"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink mb-3">Why Composability Matters</h3>
          <p class="text-muted text-sm leading-relaxed">
            A composable transaction can be immediately consumed by downstream contracts.
            A DEX trade settles, a lending protocol auto-compounds, and a yield optimizer
            rebalances &mdash; all in the same block. This is the foundation of DeFi's
            capital efficiency.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Reversibility -->
        <div class="accent-card">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center mb-4" style="background: rgba(196, 163, 90, 0.1);">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5" style="color: #c4a35a;" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M3 10h10a8 8 0 018 8v2M3 10l6 6m-6-6l6-6"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink mb-3">Why Reversibility Matters</h3>
          <p class="text-muted text-sm leading-relaxed">
            A $5 million treasury disbursement sent to the wrong address needs a recovery
            path. Institutional operations demand safety nets. Reversibility gives authorized
            signers the ability to undo a transaction before it becomes permanent.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Callout box -->
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto bg-dark rounded-xl p-6 md:p-8 border border-white/10" data-reveal>
        <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-primary/20 flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 mt-1">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 16h-1v-4h-1m1-4h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4 class="text-white font-bold mb-2">They cannot coexist in a single execution path.</h4>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              If a transaction is composable, downstream contracts can immediately build on its output.
              If that transaction were later reversed, every dependent transaction would be invalidated.
              This is not a limitation of Xhavic's design &mdash; it is a fundamental property of
              deterministic execution systems. The Dual Wallet System makes this tradeoff explicit and
              gives users the choice.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


